/-- **The theorem of the exact virtual-root certificate I3.** Let `x` be nine unit vectors of `ℝ⁴` and `(e, f)`
an orthonormal pair such that the configuration lies in the piece of the certificate (`CAP.VR.InPieceS`: the
identities of the frame, the inequalities of the cell lemma with the constants of the certificate, the cap of the
heights, the intervals of the record types and the bounds for the deviations). Then the energy
`∑ i < j, 1 / ‖x i - x j‖ ^ 2` is at least `35 / 2`. -/
theorem energy {x : Fin 9 → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4)} {e f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4)}
    (h : CAP.VR.InPieceS par heads x e f) :
    (35 : ℝ) / 2 ≤ ∑ i, ∑ j ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun j => i < j), 1 / ‖x i - x j‖ ^ 2 := by
  exact le_of_eq_of_le (by norm_num) (CAP.VR.energy_ge labels_ok checked bound_ok h)

